      "writtenOn": "2016-12-02T18:43:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, what I really meant was \"synchronous\", I will clarify in the comment.\n\nboard_set_charge_limit() will also be called from a deferred task, so a race is possible. But, the race should cause no harm. One of two current limits will end up being applied, until charge_manager_refresh() is called again (charge_manager_set_ceil() will trigger it) and the proper limit will be applied.\n\nSo in summary, charge_manager_force_ceil() allows us to shortcut the update, but is not 100% reliable.",
      "parentUuid": "cdc95346_51f7f46d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 824,
        "startChar": 0,
